---
import ComponentPage from '../../layouts/component-page.astro';

const html = `<div class="nib-empty">
  <div class="nib-empty__ghosts" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="nib-ghost">Order · item · total</div>
    <div class="nib-ghost">Order · item · total</div>
  </div>
  <p class="nib-empty__label">No orders yet</p>
  <p class="nib-empty__text">Orders appear here as soon as someone checks out.</p>
  <a class="nib-button nib-button--primary" href="#content">Share your shop</a>
</div>

<p class="nib-loading" role="status">
  <span class="nib-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>Loading products…
</p>

<label class="nib-field__label" for="e-upload">Upload</label>
<progress class="nib-progress" id="e-upload" max="100" value="40">40%</progress>

<span class="nib-media-placeholder" style="--nib-aspect: 16 / 9" role="img" aria-label="Photo loading"></span>`;
---

<ComponentPage
  title="Empty state and loading"
  lead="What a screen shows before it has content: the shape of what will come, a word, one action, and a stepping ✻."
  kind="CSS"
  code={{ html }}
>
  <div slot="example" class="el-example" set:html={html} />

  <h2>Usage</h2>
  <p>
    An empty state shows ghost rows or tiles (<code>nib-ghost</code>, dashed, labelled with what goes there), one mono
    label, one sentence and one primary action. No illustrations.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>nib-spinner</code> steps through six frames, 110ms each, in a one-character cell; put the words after it in a
    <code>nib-loading</code> live region. It is the only animation that runs on its own and it stands still under
    reduced motion. <code>nib-progress</code> styles a native <code>progress</code> as a 2px rule;
    <code>nib-media-placeholder</code> holds an image's place in its aspect ratio (<code>--nib-aspect</code>).
  </p>

  <ul slot="accessibility">
    <li>
      Wrap the spinner and its words in <code>role="status"</code> so the words are announced; the spinner itself is
      hidden.
    </li>
    <li>
      Ghost rows are decoration: hide them with <code>aria-hidden="true"</code>; the label and sentence say it.
    </li>
    <li>
      A <code>progress</code> needs a label; its value is announced by the browser.
    </li>
  </ul>
</ComponentPage>

<style>
  .el-example > :global(* + *) {
    margin-block-start: var(--nib-space-2xl);
  }

  .el-example :global(.nib-progress) {
    margin-block-start: var(--nib-space-xs);
  }
</style>
